{"name":"Chi-Gong","hex":"#d52b2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Chinese."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The twenty-second letter of the Classical and Modern Greek alphabets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chi"},{"term":"gong","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussion instrument consisting of a metal disk that emits a loud resonant sound when struck with a soft hammer.","A medal or award, particularly Knight Bachelor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make the sound of a gong; to ring a gong.","To send a signal to, using a gong or similar device.\nTo halt (originally, a contestant in a talent show; later, a performer, a speaker).\n\nTo warn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gong"}],"entries":[{"title":"Qigong","blocks":[{"text":"Qigong is a system of coordinated body-posture and movement, breathing, and meditation said to be useful for the purposes of health, spirituality, and martial arts training. With roots in Chinese medicine, philosophy, and martial arts, qigong is traditionally viewed by the Chinese and throughout Asia as a practice to cultivate and balance the mystical life-force qi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Meister_Lam_in_Jiuzhaigou2.jpg/330px-Meister_Lam_in_Jiuzhaigou2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qigong","wikidata":"Q204368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Shi_DeRu_and_Shi_DeYang.jpg/500px-Shi_DeRu_and_Shi_DeYang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Shi_DeRu_and_Shi_DeYang.jpg/1280px-Shi_DeRu_and_Shi_DeYang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki